window.docContents[186].resolve({"/StlcProp/#Type-Systems--StlcProp___-Properties-of-STLC--Uniqueness-of-Types":{"contents":"\n\nAnother nice property of the STLC is that types are unique: a\ngiven term (in a given context) has at most one type.theorem unique_types (Γ : Context) (e : Tm) (T T' : Ty)\n    (h : <{ ~Γ ⊢ ~e ⦂ ~T }>) (h' : <{ ~Γ ⊢ ~e ⦂ ~T' }>) : T = T' := by\n  sorry\n\n\n","context":"Type Systems\u0009StlcProp: Properties of STLC","header":"6.5. Uniqueness of Types","id":"/StlcProp/#Type-Systems--StlcProp___-Properties-of-STLC--Uniqueness-of-Types"}});